data: {"type": "assistant", "id": "a1", "content": "# SEO analysis: fernhill.example\n\n## The short version\n\nOrganic search brings **38% of your sessions** and grows about 4% a month, but most of it is people already searching for *Fernhill*. On the searches that bring new customers you rank at the bottom of page one.\n\n## What I found\n\n| Area | Finding | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Search Console | Property verification is broken; I used third-party ranking data instead | Fix first |\n| Speed | Mobile product pages load in 3.9 s (LCP). The hero image alone is 2.4 MB | Still failing since June |\n| Keywords | *coffee subscription* (18.1k/month) ranks 8th | Homepage still doesn't say it |\n| Backlinks | 84 referring domains vs 310 for Brewline; growth flat since March | Weak |\n| AI answers | Fernhill isn't named for *best coffee subscription uk* | Missing |\n\n## What to do, in order\n\n1. **Re-verify Search Console** (15 minutes, unblocks real query data).\n2. **Compress product images.** Expected saving is 1.6 s on mobile.\n3. **Use the word \"subscription\"** on the homepage and plan pages.\n4. **Earn links**: 41 sites link to two or more competitors and not to you. Start with the coffee blogs.\n5. **Get into listicles.** Most results for *best coffee subscription uk* are roundups, and AI answers draw on them.\n\nI've updated the SEO notes in the shared library with today's status."}
